<section class="hero"><div class="container grid"><div><div class="clientlogo"><img class="client-logo-img" alt="BMO Automation logo" src="bmo_automation_logo.png?v=20260619"></div><div class="eyebrow">Prepared for Rob Wijnen · Chief Commercial Officer</div><h1>Outbound Growth Proposal for BMO Automation</h1><p class="lead">A focused outbound campaign for precision manufacturers whose CNC machines are constrained by operator availability, frequent small-batch changeovers, low evening and weekend spindle hours, or automation tied too tightly to one machine brand. The campaign positions BMO's Multi Batch Automation, Platinum, Titanium, OptiVice, and INFINITY platform around measurable autonomous production.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#accounts">Review the 100 leads</a><a class="btn" href="#commercial">See the $1,500/month pilot</a></div><div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><strong>50</strong><span>precision-manufacturing accounts</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>100</strong><span>named stakeholder routes</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>50</strong><span>specific machining signals</span></div></div></div><aside class="visual"><div class="visualhead"><img class="client-logo-img" alt="BMO Automation logo" src="bmo_automation_logo.png?v=20260619"><div><h3>Find the lost spindle hours hiding between staffed shifts.</h3><span class="note">Outbound built around high-mix machine shops, aerospace suppliers, semiconductor equipment manufacturers, medtech producers, and machine builders where small series, one-offs, skilled-labor scarcity, and expensive idle CNC capacity create a timely BMO conversation.</span></div></div><div class="signal"><b>Multi-batch signals</b><span class="note">Identify shops where product variety and changeovers prevent conventional single-batch robot loading from producing through the night.</span></div><div class="signal"><b>Capacity without another shift</b><span class="note">Tie outreach to actual cutting hours, unattended autonomy, two-machine tending, setup time, energy timing, operator workload, and ROI.</span></div><div class="signal"><b>Independent evidence</b><span class="note">Every row connects third-party manufacturing reporting to one practical BMO capacity question.</span></div></aside></div></section>
<section><div class="container"><div class="head"><div class="eyebrow">Campaign thesis</div><h2>BMO wins when a mixed order book becomes an unattended production schedule.</h2><p>BMO is differentiated by automating small series and one-offs across turning and milling machines, rather than only repeating one large batch. The campaign gives Rob a route into manufacturers where the fastest capacity gain may come from higher spindle utilization, not another machine or another hard-to-fill shift.</p></div><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h3>Specific BMO fit</h3><p>Every rationale links a public operating signal to spindle utilization, part mix, fixtures, machine compatibility, operator time, and autonomous production.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Two-person account path</h3><p>Each row includes named leadership and operations routes, with manager or VP-level contacts prioritized for larger organizations.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Evidence-led outreach</h3><p>Each account advances toward a real order-book review, autonomy calculation, cell-fit discussion, or spindle-hour audit.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="accounts"><div class="container"><div class="head"><div class="eyebrow">100 Leads</div><h2>50 fresh machining and precision-manufacturing targets. 100 operations, production, engineering, and people routes.</h2><p>This list is separate from the previous lead list and focuses on Dutch, German, Belgian, UK, and Swiss companies with high-mix CNC production. LinkedIn buttons use exact person-and-company searches for resilience. Employment and titles should still be reconfirmed immediately before campaign launch because public roles can change.</p></div><div class="controls"><input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Search company, contact, reasoning, signal, or outreach..."><select id="signal"><option value="">All signal types</option></select><button class="btn primary" id="csv">Download CSV</button><span class="count" id="count"></span></div><div class="tablebox"><table><thead><tr><th>Company</th><th>Website</th><th>Specific BMO Fit</th><th>Contact 1 + Position</th><th>Contact 2 + Position</th><th>Buyer Signal + Source</th><th>Personalized Outreach Angle</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section class="quality" id="quality"><div class="container"><div class="head"><div class="eyebrow">Buyer-signal quality</div><h2>Specific enough to open a CNC-capacity conversation.</h2><p>The logic does not claim an active buying project. It connects third-party manufacturing evidence to a precise spindle-hour, small-series, operator-time, machine-loading, or autonomous-production question Rob can use.</p></div><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h3>Named outside sources</h3><p>Signals come from machining and manufacturing outlets, interviews, and independent workforce reporting.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>BMO relevance</h3><p>Every rationale connects the signal to Multi Batch Automation, brand-independent cells, machine utilization, fixtures, or unattended output.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Distinct outreach</h3><p>Each account uses its own operating context and a different practical first step rather than a generic automation message.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section><div class="container"><div class="founder"><img alt="Noah Levy, Founder of Beespoke Outbound" src="noah_levy_headshot.png?v=20260617"><div><div class="eyebrow">Founder · Beespoke Outbound</div><h2>Research-led outbound, built by Noah Levy.</h2><p class="lead">Beespoke builds focused outbound systems for technical B2B companies. The approach combines account research, buyer-signal mapping, concise cold email, and LinkedIn outreach to create qualified conversations without overclaiming intent.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section id="commercial"><div class="container"><div class="head"><div class="eyebrow">Commercial proposal</div><h2>A focused three-month outbound pilot.</h2></div><div class="commercial"><article class="price"><h3>Cold Email + LinkedIn Outbound</h3><div class="money">$1,500<span>/month</span></div><ul><li>Lead research and title verification before launch</li><li>Targeting and segmentation</li><li>Account-specific messaging</li><li>Campaign setup and outbound execution</li><li>Follow-up and weekly optimization</li></ul></article><article class="price"><h3>What this is not</h3><div class="money">Not<span> generic lead gen</span></div><p>This is not a scraped contact list. It is outbound infrastructure built around precision-machining accounts, third-party operating signals, and credible reasons to discuss Multi Batch Automation, higher spindle utilization, unattended production, small-series flexibility, machine compatibility, and ROI.</p><ul><li>Not a generic cold email campaign</li><li>Not a random company scrape</li><li>Not claiming unverified active automation projects or procurement cycles</li><li>Built around account intelligence</li><li>Useful before the first call</li></ul></article></div></div></section>
